      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Forme of Cury\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by the Chief Master-Cook of King Richard II, c1390 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#cury-1390\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003ECury 1390\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EGYNGAWDRY\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nTake the powche [swim bladder?] and the lyver of haddok, codlyng and hake and of oother fisshe, parboil them, take them and dice them small, take of the self broth and wine, a layour of bread of \u003Ca href=\u0022galantine.html\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003Egalyntyne\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E with good powders and salt, cast that fysshe therein and boile it. \u0026 do thereto amydoun \u0026 colour it grene.\u003Cbr\u003E"
